<title>NETHERLANDS: OCE SEEN REPLACING CSM IN DUTCH AEX INDEX.</title>
<headline>OCE SEEN REPLACING CSM IN DUTCH AEX INDEX.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Options Exchange said on Monday that indicative weightings of trade in Dutch shares showed that stock of food group CSM might be replaced by copier maker Oce-van der Grinten in Amsterdam's AEX index of most actively traded shares at the beginning of 1997.</p>
<p>Given the stocks' bourse turnovers and market capitalisations until October 1 of this year, CSM shares might be relegated to Amsterdam's so-called Midcap or AMX index for medium-sized companies which now includes Oce's shares.</p>
<p>If the current year's trends continue, the shares of software group Baan , high-technology firm ASM Lithography and technical wholesaler Otra will ascend into the AMX index from next year.</p>
<p>They are seen replacing the stock of retailer Macintosh, textiles firm Gamma and supermarkets chain De Boer Winkelbedrijven .</p>
<p>The new composition of Amsterdam's AEX and AMX share indices will be announced early next year and will be based on bourse trade figures for the full-year 1996.</p>
